WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.220
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this week was
the Agents Of SHIELD finale and I’d say

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:12.570
about half the questions we all had were answered,
some they’re teasing for Season 2 and then

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.640
in the last 15 minutes a whole mess of new
questions came up.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.040
Because Season 2 was already confirmed here’s
what I’m going to do.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.360
I’ll start with top 5 moments, then do my
review and then do some theorycrafting on

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.360
Season 2 based on what we know.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.250
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Marvel videos every week.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.700
Now that SHIELD is on hiatus Tuesdays will
be Star Wars and Marvel Movie videos.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.980
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
leave me suggestions for bonus vids.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.640
So careful for spoilers from the episode if
you haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.149
Here are my top 5 moments, Number 5 - Fitz
Sacrifices Himself For Simmons

00:00:45.149 --> 00:00:49.359
I feel like the sacrifice means more when
it’s not a superhero.

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:51.120
Like when Thor jumps into a hurricane.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.780
You’re 99 percent sure he’s going to escape
without a scratch on him.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.319
But drowning at the bottom of the ocean and
confessing your love for someone is just so

00:00:58.319 --> 00:00:59.739
much more meaningful.

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:03.609
They kept talking about life on the bottom
of the ocean I half expected some atlanteans

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:05.040
to swim up and save them.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.670
But I think that was just an easter egg.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.049
Coulson took more chances with his life, but
since he’s already been proven unkillable,

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:14.229
Fitz made the biggest sacrifice in the episode.

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:16.759
And as a result is paying the biggest price.

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:25.729
It sounds like his character, when he does
come back is going to be fundamentally different.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:28.000
Number 4 - Nick Fury Saves The Day

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.049
He got an introduction in the episode befitting
his level of badassery.

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:35.810
If you’re confused about the timeline between
the end of Winter Soldier and now, it’s

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.109
basically moving in real time.

00:01:37.109 --> 00:01:38.979
So it’s only been a couple months.

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:43.560
Fury formally quit SHIELD, or what’s left
of it and is pursuing the remnants of HYDRA

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.560
personally.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.289
In the episode he really felt like he was
walking onto a holodeck, like he knew nothing

00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:50.490
would hurt him.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.880
I loved his call out to the one man speech.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.630
One man can be Part, Part of Something Greater.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.579
When he left at the end too and said I’m
everywhere, it was the writers leaving room

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:05.729
for him to cameo on the show again next season.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:09.110
It’s funny the way Marvel never throws characters
away.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.360
Which actually ties in to my next moment.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.050
Number 3 - Coulson Takes Down Garrett

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.050
More like liquifies him with the Tesseract
Gun.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:21.390
This was just like the moment at the end of
Avengers where the Hulk thrashes Loki around.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.980
Garrett has this moment of evil triumph like
he thinks he’s escaped and bam, you get

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.010
that Joss Whedon head jerk to Coulson.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:31.710
I just love how nonchalant he is about the
whole moment to, it just completely subverts

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.530
our expectations and that’s why it’s so
good.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.620
It was moments like that early in the Marvel
Movie Universe that made Coulson such a fan

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.620
favorite.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.260
Just him casually reacting to extreme situations.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.870
Oh Asgardian Robot killing everything in the
desert, hmm.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:51.380
The only bad part is that those types of things
spoil us, and because you can’t do them

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:55.031
every week I get bummed out it’s going to
be Guardians of The Galaxy before we get to

00:02:55.031 --> 00:02:56.920
see something like that again.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.160
Actually technically that’s November, SHIELD
will be back before then.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.690
So let’s say the Season 2 premiere before
we get another “Coulson Reacts” moment.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.970
Quick side note too.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.920
We now know that the Tesseract gun is more
powerful than the Destroyer Gun.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.180
Number 2 - Skye Is An Important Part of The
Evolution

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:17.750
We didn’t get an official answer one way
or the other, but Raina and Garrett mentioned

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.250
the words evolution and becoming something
greater in almost every scene they were in.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:26.701
I’m going to save some of the theories for
the season 2 part of this video, but I love

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:31.290
the way the show is doing this crazy cosmic
comic book rhetoric in a way that allows them

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.970
to not have to show it to us.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.820
I actually kept expecting Garrett to morph
into something else after Deathlok smashed

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.820
him.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.790
Earlier when he said this is the beginning
of the end he was talking about throwing things

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.950
into the next stage of evolution.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:48.930
That really made me think Terrigen Mists and
Inhumans, because something similar happened

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.870
in the Marvel Infinity comic book last year.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.680
And Marvel is trying to develop an Inhumans
movie at some point.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.770
And Skye’s Father at the end.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.200
He and Raina and Skye all make me think that
there are multiple types of new aliens on

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.460
the show.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:11.190
The problem is it all depends on whether an
Inhuman would be able to take a transfusion

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:16.560
from a Kree, a la TAHITI Blue Alien.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.840
For the sake of argument let’s say maybe,
but Raina is probably an Inhuman.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:25.430
The term Monster just fits so well, since
sometimes inhumans turn into physically monstrous

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:28.070
looking things when they inhale the Mists.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:37.380
So in a way, SHIELD is setting up multiple
big galactic things in a really subtle way.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.250
The show doesn’t cross over with the movies
very often.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.600
But both influence each other.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.970
So things that happen on SHIELD will have
an impact on the plot of movies.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:49.850
Number 1 - Fury Tasks Coulson With Rebuilding
Shield

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:54.290
I suspected this might be the case, but I
never predicted Coulson would become director

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.350
of SHIELD.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:02.070
That black box is going to be the maguffin
of Season 2, we can talk about that in a sec.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.530
But we found out they have another new secret
base with another Patton Oswalt.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.430
I’m going to go ahead and say Life Model
Decoy.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:15.650
Wouldn’t it be funny if there was a copy
in ever single one of the super secret Nick

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.940
Fury Black Sites.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:21.590
Just 50 or 60 Patton Oswalts playing video
games in the dark by themselves.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.320
Or maybe a massive Call of Duty Lan Party.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:29.360
I think my favorite quote from the episode
was Garrett saying I’m the key to the future

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.330
of the Universe.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.330
But now it’s your turn.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.050
Let me know what your favorite moment or moments
were.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.050
It’s hard to pick.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:43.000
But I felt a lot of Whedonverse mojo in this.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:47.090
Overall the episode was a solid A. Definitely
a high point for the season.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:51.250
Bill Paxton was a breath of fresh air for
the show and I’m only sorry he didn’t

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.390
come on sooner.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:55.100
I think that was mostly because when they
started.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.639
The show only had a six episode commitment.

00:05:56.639 --> 00:05:58.970
So they didn’t even know if they’d get
renewed.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:02.490
They even shot the first three episodes before
episode 1 ever aired.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:05.880
So they didn’t even get feedback from the
fandom until they were mid-way through the

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.560
first half of the season.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.710
But now that the heavy lifting task of developing
the core team members is over.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.970
The show can start to have some more fun and
get even more meta.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.000
I love what they did with Ward’s character.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Brett Dalton is still growing on me, his fight
with May is the perfect metaphor for how most

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.730
people reacted to him until we learned he
was Hydra.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:31.430
It was like he was trolling us the whole time
with the vanilla quarterback routine.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:34.880
Coulson was already a great character when
the show started.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:39.580
But now that we’ve got to know him so much
better he’s so much more complex.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.540
Before Agents of SHIELD he was essentially
the setup man for Tony Stark jokes.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:48.390
Which isn’t a bad job, but Nick Fury named
him as a core Avenger in this episode.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:55.800
So Marvel and Disney just made Coulson as
important as Captain America and Iron Man.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.310
I don’t think that means we’ll ever see
a Coulson movie, but I’m totally fine with

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.310
that.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:05.770
A lot of the credit this season goes to Jed
Whedon and Maurissa Tancheron.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.360
They really did most of the work this season.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.680
A lot of people realize that even though Joss
Whedon was involved in getting this show off

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:12.680
the ground.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:16.490
They were the ones that ran the show all season
while he was away working on Avengers 2.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.540
So if you really like the show.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.400
They’re the ones to thank.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.130
When it was announced SHIELD got renewed for
Season 2 they even posted themselves dancing

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:28.050
crazy on instagram, so high fives to them.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.669
Now it’s time for some Theorycrafting on
Season 2.

00:07:30.669 --> 00:07:33.930
So everybody start scanning dialogue and easter
eggs again.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:39.169
First off, the plot.

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:43.080
That little black box Fury gave Coulson will
be where most of their ideas for missions

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.180
come from.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.949
They used it to find their new base.

00:07:45.949 --> 00:07:50.830
So they’re going to just keep “finding”
interesting things in that database to investigate.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.050
Just because Patton Oswalt was in the base
when they arrived doesn’t mean he’ll be

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:56.229
in every episode, but he’ll definitely cameo
again.

00:07:56.229 --> 00:08:00.560
They’re probably going to spend most of
their time on the plane traveling places.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.490
As for the rest of the team, Triplett is probably
going to replace Ward as the muscle man for

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.980
a little while.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:07.220
But Brett Dalton isn’t off the show.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.210
Ward will still be a main cast member.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.330
Coulson said they’d use him to get HYDRA
intel.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:16.650
So either they’re going to permanently house
him inside that special room on the plane,

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.770
or they’ll keep him locked up at that base.

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.040
My money is on them keeping him close by.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.920
So Ming Na can slap him around once a week.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.940
Fitz is the big question mark right now.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.400
They made it sound like he’d lost some brain
function.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:34.019
So maybe part of his arc next season will
be learning how to be a team member when he’s

00:08:34.019 --> 00:08:35.710
not super smart anymore.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:38.469
Like learning to contribute and be special
in a new way.

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:41.669
He’s not off the show either, so he’s
definitely still on the team.

00:08:41.669 --> 00:08:45.750
Garrett is definitely a puddle of goo, so
he won’t be the villain again.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.339
That honor will probably fall to Skye’s
mystery Father.

00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:48.339
The Inhuman.

00:08:48.339 --> 00:08:49.470
He’s definitely not a Kree.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:52.959
That’s funny too, because the macguffin
this season was the super blood and on Arrow

00:08:52.959 --> 00:08:54.000
it was the mirakuru.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.160
And next season it looks like SHIELD’s villain
will be Skye’s Father and on Arrow it looks

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.490
like Thea’s father or Felicity’s father
might be the villain.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.660
I know they’re not copying each other, but
the similarities in story elements is just

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.660
too weird to not think about.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:02.660
Moving on to Skye’s heritage.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:06.689
Like I just said, Raina, who I suspect is
an Inhuman who hasn’t taken in the Mists

00:09:06.689 --> 00:09:09.381
of Terrigen, has a pre-existing relationhip
with Skye’s father.

00:09:09.381 --> 00:09:11.029
Who did not look like that Blue Kree alien.

00:09:11.029 --> 00:09:14.439
Ergo, my best theory right now is that she
is an Inhuman.

00:09:14.439 --> 00:09:16.140
But she’s not like a princess or anything.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:20.529
Black Bolt is still king of the Inhumans and
that guy did not look like Black Bolt.

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:21.749
He seemed pretty evil.

00:09:21.749 --> 00:09:25.010
And in case you couldn’t see, he was covered
in blood for unknown reasons.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:29.559
I expect this Inhumans secret to be like the
Coulson TAHITI mystery next season.

00:09:29.559 --> 00:09:34.629
It’s going to take most of the season for
the show to fully explain it.

00:09:34.629 --> 00:09:39.670
Let me know what your big theories for season
2 are and if you agree that Skye is an Inhuman

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.399
based on all the evidence.

00:09:41.399 --> 00:09:48.040
So next week I’ll be doing Marvel Movie
videos and Star Wars on tuesday.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:52.760
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
leave me suggestions for bonus videos.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:56.119
Tomorrow is the Arrow Finale and the first
Flash trailer.

00:09:56.119 --> 00:09:59.939
If you check the description I posted a link
to my master video schedule so you can find

00:09:59.939 --> 00:10:05.209
out when I’m posting stuff.

